t for Lucy who always  believes that it's October 13th the date  of her injury Lucy's brother and father  go to considerable efforts to recreate  the same event for her every day with  the help of the owners of a local cafe  which is where she meets Adam Sandler's  Henry Henry falls in love with Lucy and  devises a way to help her to move on to  the next day by making her watch a recap  film of her life up until the moment she  wakes up although the ending seems  perfectly wholesome and heartening the  implications are more distressing when  you really think about them Lucy who is  revealed to have a child with Henry at  the end of the film would have had to  wake up every single day for nine months  not knowing she was pregnant let alone  waking up on a boat beside a stranger  not to mention the fact that Henry is  going to have to spend most of his life  painstakingly editing and updating her  recap videos it's not exactly ideal the  plot of Toy Story culminates with Woody  and Buzz joining forces with SIDS  mistreated and disfigured toys in order  to teach the human bully a lesson as Sid  is about to send Buzz flying into the  air using a firework Woody speaks to Sid  directly through his pre-programmed  voice box seriously deviating from his  usual lines  this acts as a cue for since toys to  crawl up to him slowly in creepy Night  of the Living Dead fashion heightening  sits horror the scene reaches its apex  when Woody bursts out from his toy form  and tells Sid so play nice  Sid screams and runs away as the toys  rejoice in their Newfound Freedom great  right well while Sid getting his long  overdue comeuppance seems fitting for a  kids movie adults will notice that Sid  now has to live with the guilt of having  tortured living things since toys are  constantly present in our culture  existing in nearly every home and Retail  establishment seeing a seemingly  innocent little toy will most likely  trigger painful reminders for him  reminders that these things 